{
 "tickets": [
  {
   "body": "Hello, I am trying to figure out where we are supposed to set up our routine data back-ups and compliance archiving rules. Our compliance officer asked me to download some older historical data exports, but when I look under the administration menu, I am completely lost on which buttons to click. Could someone please point me to where the business associate agreements and storage schedule settings are kept? Sorry to bother you with this.",
   "id": "gen-371",
   "subject": "Question about compliance archives and backup schedules"
  },
  {
   "body": "Hi support team, we need to start tracking some recent claim denials and figure out how to attach the necessary clinical notes for appeals. Could you please let me know which reporting section handles denial trends? Thanks for your help.",
   "id": "gen-372",
   "subject": "Tracking claim denials and submitting appeals"
  },
  {
   "body": "Hello, sorry to bother you, but I am trying to handle an out-of-stock medication alert for a patient and I cannot find where the pharmacy substitution messaging workflow is. Could someone help me out?",
   "id": "gen-373",
   "subject": "Out-of-stock medication alert question"
  },
  {
   "body": "This is a total disaster for our morning clinic. None of our doctors can process pharmacy out-of-stock alerts or switch any prescriptions over to alternative medications right now. Every time someone clicks on the substitution drop-down menu, the entire screen freezes up or throws a blank error code. We have a full waiting room and providers are completely stalled. Please look into this immediately.",
   "id": "gen-374",
   "subject": "CRITICAL: Medication substitution module completely frozen"
  },
  {
   "body": "Hello, sorry to bother you, but the front desk is having trouble running a state prescription monitoring program query for a patient today. Could you check our access errors?",
   "id": "gen-375",
   "subject": "Prescription monitoring query error"
  },
  {
   "body": "Hi, I am not sure what happened here, but a prescription was sent out with the wrong medication or amount, and now we need help fixing it. Can you advise?",
   "id": "gen-376",
   "subject": "Wrong medication sent on prescription"
  },
  {
   "body": "We are having a terrible morning here because the prescription refill and medication substitution system keeps crashing across all of our workstations. Every time our providers try to respond to a pharmacy out-of-stock notification, the system kicks them out entirely. We cannot send any alternative medications to pharmacies right now. Please fix this quickly so we can get back to work.",
   "id": "gen-377",
   "subject": "Medication substitution system crashing continuously"
  },
  {
   "body": "I am beyond frustrated trying to update our pharmacy directory this morning. One of our local pharmacies changed locations, and when I went into the settings to modify their address and add a custom entry, the system wouldn't let me save the changes. I tried searching for the new address three different times, cleared my browser cache, and even logged out and back in, but it just keeps spinning and giving me a generic database error. Please tell me how to fix this so our medical assistants can send prescriptions to the right place.",
   "id": "gen-378",
   "subject": "Cannot update pharmacy directory or add custom pharmacy"
  },
  {
   "body": "Hello, I am so sorry to reach out about this, but we are trying to understand how our patient portal visibility and diagnostic result release rules operate. Several patients have called asking why their lab reports and visit summaries are not showing up on their portal dashboard yet. I went into the administration settings and looked under portal configurations, but I am confused about how to set up or adjust the delayed release timers for sensitive test results. Could someone please walk me through where those timer options are located or send me a quick guide? Apologies again for taking up your time.",
   "id": "gen-379",
   "subject": "Question regarding lab result release rules and portal timers"
  },
  {
   "body": "I am extremely frustrated with the billing module today. Every single time I try to batch and generate insurance claims for electronic submission to our clearinghouse, the validation checker blocks them with cryptic error codes that make zero sense. I have spent the last two hours trying to figure out what these validation errors mean, and your help documentation has been completely useless. I need someone to tell me step-by-step how to clear these validation issues so I can get our claims submitted before the daily deadline.",
   "id": "gen-380",
   "subject": "Frustrated with claim validation errors blocking submission"
  }
 ]
}
